                <pb facs="0274" n="266" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg266"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.1121 Fernandez, Antonio/150: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Then in France, to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">St.
                                Jean de Luz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-01-31T13:00:00+00:00">January 31, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 31—10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>435. Despatch [<hi rendition="#italic">Instruction</hi>] No. 502, January 19. In
                    all dealings with rebel authorities have used effect on public opinion as our
                    most effective weapon. Am informing Sangroniz today by courier of pledge of
                    non-participation in propaganda if the Fernandezes are pardoned.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
